KNOWNBUG
contract.sol
--contract C --solidity-max-tx 1
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
`b == bytes32(uint256(b))` is a Solidity tautology and the model refutes it,
because the ABI bytesN argument's `.length` is left as free as its `.data` and
`bytes_static_equal` returns false outright on a length mismatch.

Marked KNOWNBUG rather than fixed: the pinning fix was implemented, measured to
work, and REVERTED because it cost the counterexample its recoverability and
made the generated-test funnel worse on D11_Bytes32Equality (3 cases / 0 merges
-> 1 case / 1 merge). See the contract header and the reverted branch's comment
in solidity_convert_call.cpp for what a real fix has to satisfy.
